# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
sc_api_key.txt

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other people's data
#
# sc-watch.db holds reputation judgements about named real players, and
# rsi_cache.db holds their profiles. sightings.csv is the same data as a log.
# audit/ is screenshots of other players' HUD labels. None of it belongs in a
# repository, in a release, or in a copy handed to anyone.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
sc-watch.db
sc-watch.db.bak-*
rsi_cache.db
sightings.csv
audit/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local configuration: keybinds, monitor index, API mode, audio voice.
# Machine-specific, and settings.json is the file the UI writes.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
settings.json
housekeeping.json
audio.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capture output. Frames are ~11 MB each and these directories reached 1.1 GB
# during development.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
frames/
live_frames/
debug_bursts/
probe_frames/
detections/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated at first run
#
# The tones are deterministic WAVs that audio.py writes if tones/ is empty, so
# they are not committed - but they ARE kept in the working folder, because a
# packaged build should ship them rather than write into its install directory
# the first time it speaks.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
restart.flag
tones/*.wav
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
#
# sc-watch.spec is NOT ignored - it is how the release is built. The wildcard
# that used to cover it would have left every clone unable to produce a build.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
.venv-build/
